# requests/confirm.http
#
# WHAT THIS IS
# Tests for the whole email confirmation flow (B3).
# Needs the "REST Client" extension + `npm run dev` running.
#
# HOW TO USE
# Some tests need a token. Tokens are printed in the terminal running
# `npm run dev`, inside the EMAIL box, after "confirm?token=".
# Copy everything after "token=" and paste it into the matching
# variable below, then SAVE this file before sending the next test.

@base = http://localhost:3000

# Paste tokens here as you go (no quotes, no spaces)
@prospectToken = lQByIN91BsqIxoUi485X5EkRDCVZh5nWIgpDsma6qug
@scoutOldToken = WSjncZBfY7FkYsAWfiHehdzKX1mpMTWOUOioNWM60kY
@scoutNewToken = 652tqos19WnYjMgVxmOtR3YKc5GoG0rat62vbPoaQWQ
@lateToken = LbM7xULIIvjNX-vwc_UQhlNfF09zxMu4RloRsGUVG2o
@late2Token = rhsFtb2J5fdLas18FX2erP__f2C2Dza4RQpwmGttzek
### 1. Sign up a prospect → 201. Then copy its token into @prospectToken
POST {{base}}/api/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "prospect",
  "email": "tester1@example.com",
  "displayName": "tester1",
  "platform": "twitch",
  "channelUrl": "twitch.tv/tester1",
  "ageConfirmed": true
}

### 2. Press Enter WITHOUT ticking the rules → 400 "rules_required"
POST {{base}}/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{prospectToken}}" }

### 3. Press Enter WITH the rules ticked → 200 "confirmed", number 1
POST {{base}}/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{prospectToken}}", "rulesAccepted": true }

### 4. Press Enter again → 200 "already_confirmed", same number
POST {{base}}/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{prospectToken}}", "rulesAccepted": true }

### 5. Sign up again with the same email → 409 "already on the list"
POST {{base}}/api/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "prospect",
  "email": "TESTER1@example.com",
  "displayName": "tester1",
  "platform": "twitch",
  "channelUrl": "twitch.tv/tester1",
  "ageConfirmed": true
}

### 6. Sign up a scout → 201. Copy its token into @scoutOldToken
POST {{base}}/api/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "scout",
  "email": "scout1@example.com",
  "displayName": "Big Creator",
  "platformUrls": ["tiktok.com/@bigcreator"],
  "audienceSize": "50k_100k",
  "contentTypes": ["streaming"],
  "ageConfirmed": true,
  "scoutOffers": ["feedback"],
  "scoutHours": "3_5",
  "commitmentAccepted": true  
}

### 7. Scout signs up again before confirming → 200 "resent". Copy the NEW token into @scoutNewToken
POST {{base}}/api/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "scout",
  "email": "scout1@example.com",
  "displayName": "Big Creator",
  "platformUrls": ["tiktok.com/@bigcreator"],
  "audienceSize": "50k_100k",
  "contentTypes": ["streaming"],
  "ageConfirmed": true,
  "scoutOffers": ["feedback"],
  "scoutHours": "3_5",
  "commitmentAccepted": true
}

### 8. Use the OLD scout link → 400 "invalid" (the new email replaced it)
POST {{base}}/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{scoutOldToken}}" }

### 9. Use the NEW scout link (scouts don't need the rules tick) → 200 "confirmed", scout number 1
POST {{base}}/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{scoutNewToken}}" }

### 10. A made-up token → 400 "invalid"
POST {{base}}/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "thisIsNotARealTokenAtAll123" }

### 11. Sign up someone who'll let their link expire → 201. Copy the token into @lateToken,
#     then run this in pgAdmin to fake 48 hours passing:
#     UPDATE signups SET confirm_expires_at = NOW() - INTERVAL '1 hour' WHERE email = 'late@example.com';
POST {{base}}/api/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "prospect",
  "email": "late@example.com",
  "displayName": "latey",
  "platform": "kick",
  "channelUrl": "kick.com/latey",
  "ageConfirmed": true
}

### 12. Expired link → 410 "expired"
POST {{base}}/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "{{lateToken}}", "rulesAccepted": true }

### Test 13: sign up a prospect we'll "age" with SQL
# Expect: 201 created, and a confirm email printed in the terminal
POST http://localhost:3000/api/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "prospect",
  "email": "late2@example.com",
  "displayName": "latey2",
  "ageConfirmed": true,
  "platform": "twitch",
  "channelUrl": "twitch.tv/latey2",
  "streamCategory": "GTA RP"
}

### Test 14: confirm with an expired link
# Before sending, run this in pgAdmin (Query Tool on streamerdraft):
#   UPDATE signups SET confirm_expires_at = NOW() - INTERVAL '1 hour' WHERE email = 'late2@example.com';
# Expect: 410 "This link has expired..."
POST http://localhost:3000/api/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{late2Token}}",
  "rulesAccepted": true
}